---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Home">
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <p>
      Welcome to Leon's history notes - a repository for my notes as I learn
      history as an amateur historian.
    </p>

    <p>
      I'm organizing my notes based on a <span class="font-bold">period</span> (for
      example Neolithic, Imperial Antiquity, Long 19th Century, etc.) and <span
        class="font-bold"
      >
        location
      </span> (Egypt, Mesopotamia, ...). For each period and location I note down
      important events, people, locations, religion, etc. and attach times to them.
    </p>

    <p>
      I built this site to make notes more navigable - in a typical
      bullet-points style note app, things can quickly become hard to view and
      revise. In this site, notes will be viewable through multiple
      perspectives: period based (what happened in this period accross the
      world?), location based (what happened in Egypt over time?) and map based
      (show events on the map).
    </p>

    <p>
      It's still early days - for now, only a few note exist, and they can only
      be viewed in a flat bullet point view. I will keep updating the site with
      new features and notes as I progress through this journey of learning all
      of world's history.
    </p>

    <div class="flex gap-4">
      <a href="/explore" class="underline text-md font-semibold">
        Explore Notes
      </a>

      <a href="/news" class="underline text-md font-semibold">News</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
